<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Order of the Sun of Peru</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1821">1821</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Order of the Sun</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Order of the Sun of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peru">Peru</a> is the country's highest state decoration, founded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jose-de-san-martin">José de San Martín</a> on 8 October 1821 to reward those who served the cause of independence. Abolished in 1825, it was restored in 1921, and it is regarded as the oldest civil and military order in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/americas">Americas</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/order-of-the-sun-of-peru.jpg" alt="Order of the Sun of Peru" width="320" height="447" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Orden_del_Sol.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
